Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Claude connects for real on the first run, and
 every AI state is told right
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A new user (Claude Desktop + a Claude Code she never signed in to) said Yes
everywhere and got nothing: no Meridian in Claude Desktop, Claude Code left at
"Sign in…" deep in Settings, Improve with AI dead.

- The newest copy of an agent CLI runs (ai/cli_versions): an old Claude Code
  in /usr/local/bin no longer wins over the current one in ~/.local/bin, so
  sign-in isn't misread. Its sign-in runs that copy too (a Terminal's login
  profile may list the old one first). Settings says which one, and a CLI too
  old for `auth status` says "Update needed", never "Not signed in".
- The welcome tour signs Claude Code in right after Yes and waits for it, and
  ends with an honest check: Claude Desktop verified (its bridge said hello),
  needs a restart, will load it when it opens, or failed with why; Claude Code
  signed in or Sign in now. Each with one fix button.
- Claude Desktop: the entry is put back after Claude quits (it may write its
  old copy of the file back), and Meridian refuses to connect from a download
  or disk image whose path goes away.
- Boost's Improve with AI says "Sign in to Claude to use AI" and starts it.
- Settings › Connect shows each agent's real state, read from its config the
  way Connect writes it (per Claude/Codex account), Disconnect/Reconnect, and
  the raw file or command behind Details. Account chips say Signed in / Needs
  sign-in with the Sign in on the chip.
- Tests' stand-in CLIs run in the tests' own environment, never through the
  person's login shell (whose CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR names a real config).

